<%#
  The mailing list signup.

  A plain form_tag rather than form_with: form_with emits an authenticity token,
  which has to live in the session, which would issue a session cookie to every
  anonymous reader of every public page. SubscribersController explains why
  that trade is the right way round here.

  locals:
    source — the page this appeared on, so we can tell which writing earns
             addresses. Without it every signup looks the same.
%>
<section class="subscribe">
  <h2>The monthly note</h2>

  <p>
    One useful thing a month about caring for a parent at a distance, and a line
    on what has changed in Remindly. You will also get the
    <a href="<%= routine_sheet_path %>">printable daily routine sheet</a> —
    though that one is free to anybody, list or no list.
  </p>

  <form action="<%= subscribers_path %>" method="post" class="subscribe-form">
    <input type="hidden" name="source" value="<%= source %>">

    <%# Hidden from people, irresistible to bots. Left unlabelled on purpose. %>
    <div class="honeypot" aria-hidden="true">
      <label for="website">Leave this empty</label>
      <input type="text" name="website" id="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off">
    </div>

    <label for="subscribe-email">Your email address</label>
    <div class="subscribe-row">
      <input type="email" name="email" id="subscribe-email" required
             autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com">
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Send it to me</button>
    </div>
  </form>
</section>
